# Low Water, Act 3: the last dawn. The final apportionment in two lines, Mother's fate, Lamb's fate,
# and the epilogue as the next night's lights. Director's file, 2026-10-17. Plan: design/ACT3-PLAN.md
# section 7 (draft 2). Entered from the Brine at 06:20 (brine3) or the event ev3.dawn at 06:20.

# ---- new ids
@fact dawn3.sent
@var fate_lamb
default: none
values: none, boat, keeper, typist, brine, post, road
@var fate_mother
default: dark
values: crown, keeper, bulb, automated, dark

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the room
@node dawn3.start
place: brine
cost: 2
alt: dawn3.sent.node ? has(dawn3.sent)
nar: The Brine at twenty past six: the whole town in a hull, the water a hand below the step, the stove the only dry thing, and the assessor at the table with the form.
nar: CLAIM 4471/G. FINAL APPORTIONMENT. Two lines are ruled where there used to be one.
voice: precedent: A second loss on the same policy. The Shelf anticipated it. The Shelf types what it is told. {when: has(hester.told), dc: 4}
voice: condolence: Whoever you write here wakes up in it. Some of them are in this room, standing in water. {dc: 5}
go: dawn3.one

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- line one: the dark of Low Night
@node dawn3.one
hub: yes
place: brine
nar: Line one. The dark of Low Night, twenty to ten, three nights ago.
nar: So far: the Guild. {when: has(cause3.guild)}
nar: So far: the Trust and the Board. {when: has(cause3.trust)}
nar: So far: the keeper. {when: has(cause3.keeper)}
nar: So far: the Shelf itself. {when: has(cause3.shelf)}
opt: "Malice by wreckers, as the Board filed it." -> dawn3.one.wreckers ? !has(cause3.guild) & !has(cause3.trust) & !has(cause3.keeper) & !has(cause3.shelf)
opt: "The Guild, which pulled the switch." -> dawn3.add ? !has(cause3.guild) & (has(marrow.switch) | has(afterdark.told) | has(switch.recreated) | ((has(scales.switch) | has(scales.kept)) & has(lamps.pink))) {do: set(cause3.guild)}
opt: "The Trust and the Board: the wiring, the clause, the claim." -> dawn3.add ? !has(cause3.trust) & (has(works.order) | has(works.inferred)) & (has(panel.restrike) | has(clause.struck) | has(ink.crake) | has(fisk.button)) {do: set(cause3.trust)}
opt: "The keeper, and a lens a third bottle." -> dawn3.add ? !has(cause3.keeper) & (has(prism.green_oven) | has(lens.green) | has(oven.inferred) | has(relics.counted)) & (has(coat.wenna_dry) | has(log.ahead) | has(wenna.heard_motor) | has(wenna.told_landing)) {do: set(cause3.keeper)}
opt: "The Shelf itself: a claim on an insurer that does not exist." -> dawn3.add ? !has(cause3.shelf) & has(typist.heard) + has(ropewalk.notice_matched) + has(hester.seen_typing) + has(hester.told) + has(crake.drafts) + has(pip.told) + has(e.matched) >= 2 {do: set(cause3.shelf)}
opt: "The act of the sea." -> dawn3.one.sea ? !has(cause3.guild) & !has(cause3.trust) & !has(cause3.keeper) & !has(cause3.shelf)
opt: "Rub line one out and begin it again." -> dawn3.one.rub ? has(cause3.guild) | has(cause3.trust) | has(cause3.keeper) | has(cause3.shelf)
opt: "Ink line one." -> dawn3.two ? has(cause3.guild) | has(cause3.trust) | has(cause3.keeper) | has(cause3.shelf)

@node dawn3.add
cost: 1
nar: The pencil goes on. Somebody behind the assessor reads it upside down and tells somebody else.
go: ^hub

@node dawn3.one.rub
cost: 1
do: clear(cause3.guild); clear(cause3.trust); clear(cause3.keeper); clear(cause3.shelf)
nar: The rubber goes through to the table in one place.
go: ^hub

@node dawn3.one.wreckers
cost: 2
do: set(cause3.wreckers1)
nar: Malice by wreckers, three nights ago. The words were always in the claim, dry.
voice: carbon: 22:20 on Low Night. A light in the drowned lamp, and a ferry turned away from it, not toward. Whatever happened tonight, it did not happen then. {dc: 4}
go: dawn3.two

@node dawn3.one.sea
cost: 2
do: set(cause3.sea1)
nar: The act of the sea, three nights ago. It cannot be asked a question, which is why the form has room for it.
go: dawn3.two

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- line two: the loss in the gale
@node dawn3.two
hub: yes
place: brine
nar: Line two. The loss in the gale.
nar: What was lost: Mother, put out by hand at the height of it. {when: has(loss3.mother)}
nar: What was lost: a lamp the town chose to keep, put out by hand. {when: has(loss3.lamp) & !has(loss3.mother)}
nar: What was lost: the Ellen Varty, on the Spit. {when: has(collier.spit)}
nar: What was lost: nothing the town had chosen to keep. {when: !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & !has(collier.spit)}
opt: "Malice by wreckers. This time, with names." -> dawn3.two.wreckers ? has(wreckers.real)
opt: "The Trust: the letter that asked for the claim kept open." -> dawn3.two.trust ? has(letter.kept_open) | has(crake.drafts)
opt: "The Shelf itself, which anticipated it." -> dawn3.two.shelf ? has(typist.heard) + has(ropewalk.notice_matched) + has(hester.seen_typing) + has(hester.told) + has(crake.drafts) + has(pip.told) + has(e.matched) >= 2
opt: "The act of the sea." -> dawn3.two.sea
opt: "No loss. Write the line through." -> dawn3.two.none ? !has(loss3.mother) & !has(loss3.lamp) & !has(collier.spit)

@node dawn3.two.wreckers
cost: 2
do: set(cause3.wreckers2)
nar: Malice by wreckers, in the gale, and the names under it. For the first time in three nights the claim's own words are true, and they are true about the wrong night.
go: dawn3.send

@node dawn3.two.trust
cost: 2
do: set(cause3.trust2)
nar: The Trust, which wrote at one in the morning to ask for the claim kept open through a gale.
go: dawn3.send

@node dawn3.two.shelf
cost: 2
do: set(cause3.shelf2)
nar: The Shelf, which typed FURTHER LOSS ANTICIPATED and was read aloud on the quay.
go: dawn3.send

@node dawn3.two.sea
cost: 2
do: set(cause3.sea2)
nar: The act of the sea. Tonight, at least, the sea was certainly there.
go: dawn3.send

@node dawn3.two.none
cost: 1
do: set(cause3.none2)
nar: A line ruled through. Nobody in the room has ever seen a loss adjuster write nothing on purpose.
go: dawn3.send

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the tube
@node dawn3.send
place: tube
cost: 4
do: set(dawn3.sent); quest(a3.verdict, sent)
nar: The canister goes into the brass mouth with the water at the weigh-house door. Under the town, the tube takes it to a back room on the Ropewalk, which everyone in the Brine now knows.
nar: The bell rings once.
go: dawn3.reply

@node dawn3.sent.node
go: dawn3.reply

@node dawn3.reply
place: brine
cost: 4
nar: Twenty minutes later the tube thumps. Pip brings it to the Brine through water to her knees, and reads it out, because there is no point now in not reading it.
nar: SHELF: RECEIVED. CLAIM 4471/G CLOSED. THE SHELF THANKS THE ASSESSOR FOR ELEVEN YEARS. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
nar: SHELF: RECEIVED. CLAIM 4471/G CLOSED. {when: !has(ropewalk3.wages)}
line: PIP: The e's not sticking. She's used Grandad's machine. {when: has(ropewalk3.carriage_mended)}
line: PIP: The e's sticking. It's the Trust's machine. It's always the Trust's machine. {when: !has(ropewalk3.carriage_mended)}
nar: The town takes both lines, as voted, and goes home along the wet quay to say so. {when: var.brine3.accept == whole}
nar: The town takes the first line and leaves the second on the form, as voted. Nobody in Gullet will say aloud what happened in the gale. {when: var.brine3.accept == first}
nar: The town voted to take none of it. The form goes down the tube anyway; that is what forms are for. {when: var.brine3.accept == none}
go: dawn3.mother

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mother's fate
@node dawn3.mother
cost: 1
if: true => fate_mother = dark
if: !has(cause3.trust) & !has(cause3.trust2) & mother == burning => fate_mother = automated
if: has(vote.keeper_paid) | var.brine3.keeper != none => fate_mother = keeper
if: has(mole3.bulb_fitted) => fate_mother = bulb
if: has(mole3.crown_fitted) & var.lens != broken => fate_mother = crown
if: (has(cause3.trust) | has(cause3.trust2)) & !has(vote.keeper_paid) & !has(mole3.bulb_fitted) & !has(mole3.crown_fitted) => fate_mother = automated
go: dawn3.fates

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lamb's fate
@node dawn3.fates
place: brine
cost: 3
nar: The water stops at the step, or it does not, and either way at a quarter to seven it begins, very slowly, to go out. {when: !has(surge.held)}
nar: The water stops at the step, as the Almanac said it would, and at a quarter to seven it begins, very slowly, to go out. {when: has(surge.held)}
nar: The assessor's coat hangs on the peg by the stove. It has three tide marks at the hem now.
opt: "Go down to the mole steps for the morning boat." -> dawn3.boat ? (var.fate_mother == crown | var.fate_mother == bulb | has(oldlight.lanterns) | var.brine3.kept == oldlight | has(collier.through))
opt: "Take the Alderman's launch to Hesk, as she offered." -> dawn3.launch ? !(var.fate_mother == crown | var.fate_mother == bulb | has(oldlight.lanterns) | var.brine3.kept == oldlight | has(collier.through)) & var.hill3_offer == boat
opt: "Take the bag and walk out on the coast road at first light." -> dawn3.road ? !(var.fate_mother == crown | var.fate_mother == bulb | has(oldlight.lanterns) | var.brine3.kept == oldlight | has(collier.through)) & var.hill3_offer != boat
opt: "Go up the hill and take the Alderman's post." -> dawn3.post ? var.hill3_offer == post
opt: "Take the brass key on its string, and climb." -> dawn3.keeper ? var.brine3.keeper == lamb | (has(wenna.asked) & has(vote.keeper_paid) & var.brine3.keeper != wenna)
opt: "Go to the Ropewalk, where there is a machine with a straight e." -> dawn3.typist ? has(ropewalk3.offered) | var.hill3_offer == typewriter | (has(hester.told) & has(e.matched))
opt: "Sit down at the Brine's bar and ask Sabine what is owed." -> dawn3.brine

@node dawn3.boat
place: mole_steps
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = boat
line: PENHALLOW: Log, oh-seven-hundred. Mother burning true. One passenger, Shelf. Master sails. {when: var.fate_mother == crown | var.fate_mother == bulb}
line: PENHALLOW: Log, oh-seven-hundred. A collier came through the dog-leg in a gale on the town's own lights. If they'll do for her, they'll do for me. One passenger, Shelf. Master sails. {when: var.fate_mother != crown & var.fate_mother != bulb & has(collier.through)}
line: PENHALLOW: Log, oh-seven-hundred. One passenger, Shelf. Master sails. {when: var.fate_mother != crown & var.fate_mother != bulb & !has(collier.through)}
nar: The assessor stands at the rail with the claims case on both knees, dry on the usual rate, and knowing now whose. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
nar: The assessor stands at the rail with the claims case on both knees, dry, and watches Gullet go small: the oxblood, the mustard, the teal, the bone, and a figure at the end of the mole in a coat of the same colour as the first.
go: dawn3.epilogue

@node dawn3.launch
place: mole_steps
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = boat
nar: The Trust's launch, brass and varnish, the only boat in Gullet that sails without a master's say. The Alderman does not come down to see it off. Mrs Pellow does, with a basket, and does not say what is in it.
nar: The assessor sits dry under the launch's awning and watches Mother go small behind, not burning true.
nar: The awning is the Trust's, and the brass, and the coal in the boiler. Seven shillings in the pound of the assessor, carried to Hesk at her expense one last time. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
go: dawn3.epilogue

@node dawn3.road
place: quay
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = road
nar: No boat sails this morning that will take the Shelf. The coast road goes out past the gasholder and over the hill to Hesk.
nar: The assessor walks it with the bag and the claims case, dry above the knee, and wet below, which is new.
nar: Nobody pays for the road. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
go: dawn3.epilogue

@node dawn3.post
place: crake_study
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = post
line: CRAKE: Assessor to the Trust. A salary, a desk, a lamp that does not flicker. You will be very good at it. You already know where everything is.
line: CRAKE: The same money as before. Openly, this time. You may find you prefer it. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
nar: The desk faces the window, and the window faces the harbour, and from here, by day, every colour on the quay is visible and none of them can be heard.
go: dawn3.epilogue

@node dawn3.keeper
place: stairs
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = keeper
nar: A hundred and twelve stairs. The assessor counts them going up, as she said she did, for twenty-eight years. At the top the panel, and the button, and the spray on the glass like somebody practising.
line: WENNA: You'll learn the difference. Eye shut. Not dark.
nar: The town will pay the keeper on Fridays, out of a tin at the Brine. The assessor has watched them count it, every coin, from hands the assessor knows. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
go: dawn3.epilogue

@node dawn3.typist
place: gannet_house
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = typist
nar: The back room on the Ropewalk. Two machines on the table now: the Trust's, with its bent e, pushed to one side, and an older one with every letter straight. {when: has(ropewalk3.carriage_mended)}
nar: The back room on the Ropewalk. The Trust's machine, with its bent e, and under a cloth on the dresser an older one in two pieces, waiting. {when: !has(ropewalk3.carriage_mended)}
line: HESTER: You'll want to know the usual rate. There isn't one. You make it up, and then you keep it.
nar: The first thing the assessor types on the straight machine is a line in the ledger: NIGHT ASSESSOR, HESK. The figure after it is left blank. {when: has(ropewalk3.wages)}
go: dawn3.epilogue

@node dawn3.brine
place: brine
cost: 5
do: fate_lamb = brine
line: SABINE: Three nights, a room, the stove, the oven, an egg I gave you for nothing and you know which. Call it a column. {when: var.seenas_brine == regular | rep(brine) >= 2}
line: SABINE: No column yet. A stool, then. Every column on that slate started as a stool. {when: var.seenas_brine != regular & rep(brine) < 2}
nar: She draws a little bowler hat at the head of a new column on the slate, and under it, nothing yet.
go: dawn3.epilogue

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the next night, from the hill
@node dawn3.epilogue
place: hill_lane
cost: 0
camera: wide
nar: The next night, from Chancel Hill.
nar: Mother, burning white and whole, every prism in its numbered place. {when: var.fate_mother == crown}
nar: Mother, burning green at the edges and honest, and Wenna paid to sit with her, the first wage in six years. {when: var.fate_mother == keeper & var.brine3.keeper == wenna}
nar: Mother, burning green at the edges and honest, and somebody paid to sit with her. {when: var.fate_mother == keeper & var.brine3.keeper != wenna}
nar: Mother, burning with the Old Bulb in her, a low yellow light the Congregation kneels to on the steps. {when: var.fate_mother == bulb}
nar: Mother, dark, a notice on her door, waiting for a lens from Hesk that will come in the spring or will not. {when: var.fate_mother == automated}
nar: Mother, dark; and out in the bay, low on the water, lanterns in the Old Light, hung there by the town. {when: var.fate_mother == dark & (has(oldlight.lanterns) | var.brine3.kept == oldlight)}
nar: Mother, dark. {when: var.fate_mother == dark & !has(oldlight.lanterns) & var.brine3.kept != oldlight}
nar: The post at the top of the steps. {when: var.light_steps == 1 & !has(lampout.steps)}
nar: The Brine's porthole over the bins. {when: var.light_porthole == 1 & !has(lampout.porthole)}
nar: The Gut's wires, all twelve colours. {when: var.light_gut == 1 & !has(lampout.gut)}
nar: The lamp on the town balance, which nobody owns. {when: var.light_balance == 1 & !has(lampout.balance)}
nar: The white lamps on the hill, under one of which the Alderman is walking. {when: var.light_hill == 1 & !has(lampout.hill) & !has(cause3.trust) & !has(cause3.trust2)}
nar: The white lamps on the hill, and the Alderman's house dark. {when: var.light_hill == 1 & !has(lampout.hill) & (has(cause3.trust) | has(cause3.trust2))}
nar: On the harbour office step, the Old Light's bronze lantern gear, green with a hundred years, chalked FOR THE TOWN in Nan Cockle's capitals. {when: has(oldlight.gear_saved)}
nar: Where the Old Light's bronze gear should be, nothing: it went out on the last of the eye with the men who came for it. {when: has(oldlight.gear_lost)}
nar: In the Guild hall, under the Captain's apron, a stoker off the Ellen Varty sleeps in Marrow's coat. {when: has(gut3.swimmer)}
nar: The sodium, orange, on the quay, and under it the harbourmaster, wet like everybody after the surge, for once unremarkable.
nar: Somewhere below the hill a clock in a bar is eleven minutes slow, or it is not.
nar: LOW WATER ENDS.
end: game.end
